bevy-horizon: NAK_DEBUG=stats, one line of shader statistics per shader

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at d4a00ea0ab3f59afb967cc5d779e4263d237bd77, after 0001 and 0002. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies
it; this text before the first "diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

NAK prints a shader's statistics (instruction count, GPRs, max warps per SM, spills) only under
NAK_DEBUG=print, which also prints the whole IR after every compiler pass. On the Switch, and
far more under Ryujinx, that output makes a large shader take minutes to compile, so a game
never gets as far as its world pipelines. "stats" prints only a single grep-able line per shader:

  NAK_STATS stage=fragment instrs=... static_cycles=... max_warps=... gprs=... slm=...
            spills_mem=... fills_mem=... spills_reg=... fills_reg=... tex=... txd=... tld=...
            ld=... ipa=... bra=... source=<first 4 bytes of the source BLAKE3> name=<entry point>

tex/txd/tld count texture instructions by kind (implicit LOD or level, explicit gradients,
fetches and gathers), ld counts global, local, shared and constant-buffer loads, ipa counts
fragment input interpolations and bra branches, all in the final shader. Set it per launch with
an "env NAK_DEBUG=stats" line in a game's options.txt (docs/logging-and-crash-reports.md).

